# Review routing. GitHub requests a review from the owners of any path a PR touches.
#
# The split mirrors the one CI already draws: an entry change edits data and the files
# generated from it; a code change edits the toolchain, the front end, or the deploy
# config. build.yml warns when a single PR does both, because the second is never
# reviewable on the strength of the first.
#
# With one maintainer every line points to the same person and this file does nothing.
# That is the point: adding the second maintainer is then one line per area, not a
# redesign. See GOVERNANCE.md for which merges need a second maintainer regardless.

# Default owner for anything not matched below.
*                       @yigitisik

# Editorial. The registry itself and the vocabulary that grades it.
/data/                  @yigitisik
/docs/SCHEMA.md         @yigitisik

# Toolchain and front end. Treat as code review, never as an entry review.
/scripts/               @yigitisik
/app.js                 @yigitisik
/styles.css             @yigitisik

# Deploy, CI and security posture. Changes here can disable the checks that make
# contributor PRs safe to merge, so they get the closest reading.
/.github/               @yigitisik
/vercel.json            @yigitisik
/CITATION.cff           @yigitisik
/GOVERNANCE.md          @yigitisik
